### Case: valid-call-transformed / response-really-converted
###
### Plain JSON in. The gateway converts this body to XML, calls the handler on
### <SOAP_HANDLER_PATH>, and converts the XML response back to JSON.
###
### The field names here must match the ELEMENT NAMES the SOAP handler reads. If
### they don't, you typically get a 200 with an empty result rather than an error —
### which reads as "no data" and is actually "wrong request".
###
### Expect 200, content-type application/json, AND a body with no angle brackets.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/locations
authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
content-type: application/json

{"region":"EMEA","activeOnly":true}

### curl equivalent:
###   curl -i -X POST {{GATEWAY}}/locations \
###     -H 'authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}' \
###     -H 'content-type: application/json' \
###     -d '{"region":"EMEA","activeOnly":true}'
